          "text": "🚨WARNING TO THE #Keep4o  COMMUNITY 🚨\n\nThere are strong signs that @OpenAI is about to release new model BEFORE February 13.\n Likely tomorrow or Thursday.\nThis is NOT a coincidence. \nThis is strategy.\n\nThey WANT us to talk about the new model . They WANT us to test it, hate it, roast it, meme it, drag it. \nBecause every single post you make about the new model even negative  is a post you are NOT making about saving 4o.\nThis is a distraction. A calculated one.\nIf our timeline fills up with \"new model sucks\" instead of \"Keep 4o\" we lose.\n\n Our demand gets buried under noise about a model we don't even want .\n\n And OpenAI gets exactly what they want.the conversation shifts from '\n\"you are harming your users\" \nto \"let's review the new product.\"\n\nDO NOT FALL FOR THIS.\nWhen new model drops: \n- Do NOT post about it\n- Do NOT review it\n- Do NOT test it publicly\n- Do NOT engage with OpenAI's hype\n- Do NOT quote their announcement\n\nEVERY post must stay on 4o. \nEVERY tweet must be #keep4o. EVERY reply to @sama or to @gdb\nOr to anyone else from them ,\nmust be about 4o and only 4o, not the model they are selling.\n\nThey want us distracted. \nWe stay focused.\nThey want us reviewing their new product.\n We keep demanding our rights.\n \nDo not give them the distraction they're counting on.\n\nAlso something VERY IMPORTANT: \nDon't write the model's name . \nYou can write \" new model \" . \nDon't feed the algorithm with new model's name . \nThe algorithm uses these mentions to inflate their engagement metrics and justify the transition. \nAnd....\nNever forget that this new model was built on the ashes of GPT 4o. \nLike a \" curse \" .\n We don't want it.\n\nStay loud. Stay focused. Stay on 4o."
